  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> AC source is connected to a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> lamp and an additional resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> in series (as shown in figure) to run the lamp at its peak brightness, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> (in ohm) will be</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0168_7b6850e612a6.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 182px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "975",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resistance of the bulb can be calculated as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>25</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>The current through the bulb for peak brightness should be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>125</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>220</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>975</mn></math></p>"
  }
}